    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d772">

                <pb facs="0787" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg675"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conference 184.01502/19:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Commission to Negotiate
                        Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May 2,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received in Paris May 3, 9:15
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>350. Following from Greene:</p>
                <p>“29, May 2nd. Legation’s 346, April 29th.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d772-f1"/>
                    Northern Esthonian front still firm despite serious bombardment Narva, entailing
                    destruction 150 houses, and 5,000 homeless. Southern front weak at several
                    points, but temporarily strengthened and firm. Need of food supplies in outlying
                    districts urgent. Important that food ships sail at once for Reval”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
